-- TOPIC 1:- CHAR vs VARCHAR
   -- We use CHAR when the length is predictable and fixed. 
      "CHAR always uses the maximum space we set, filling empty slots with spaces."
   -- Example :-  'ZIPCODE', 'abbrevations'
   -- We use VARCHAR when the length is variable. It saves a massive amount of disk space.
      "VARCHAR shrinks to use only the exact space our text needs."
-- Example :-  'Name', 'email id', 'address'
   -- Let say we entering data 'RAM'
   -- CHAR(6) sees "RAM" (3 characters) and says: "I must fill my box." 
      It adds 3 invisible spaces to the end.
      It saves "RAM   " and uses all 6 bytes of storage.

   -- VARCHAR(6) sees "RAM" (3 characters) and says: "I will shrink to fit."
      "I will shrink to fit." It saves just "RAM" and uses 4 bytes of storage 
       (3 bytes for the letters + 1 extra byte to remember the length is 3).

